text\n\n## Description\n...resolve whether the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin's workspace resolution and the kubernetes:// workspace store can be initialized and exercised in an artifacts-only MLflow server where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized. The answer determines the scope of the plugin work and the server's initialization sequence for workspace-aware artifact serving.\n\n## Scope\n- Trace the plugin's workspace resolution initialization path (WorkspaceStoreRegistry / mlflow.workspace_provider entry point group) and identify any dependency on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n- Determine whether the kubernetes:// workspace store resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking stores.\n- Determine whether artifact request paths under the artifacts endpoints carry sufficient information (experiment/run identifiers) to resolve workspace membership for the standard S3 artifact path structure.\n- Record a bounded outcome: resolution works in the artifacts-only context as-is, or workspace resolution is coupled to full server initialization and requires factoring into an independent initialization path.\n- Deliverable: findings document with cited source evidence and a refactor-or-verify determination that gates the plugin and server implementation work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The findings document states, with file-level source evidence, whether the plugin's workspace resolution initialization depends on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n- The findings document states whether the kubernetes:// workspace store can resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping without initialized tracking stores, with evidence.\n- The findings document records the bounded outcome and the exact coupling points (if any) that would require refactoring, so the plugin and server implementation scope can be finalized.\n- Artifact request path structure is confirmed (or refuted) to carry experiment/run identifiers sufficient for workspace resolution under the standard S3 artifact store layout.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-1 (P0)... — enables\n- HLR-2 (P0)... — enables\n- HLR-7 (P1)...\n\nHmm, HLR Traceability section in epic: \"which strategy HLRs this epic covers\". For investigations, they gate/enable HLRs. I'll phrase \"Enables/gates\".\n\n---\n\n**E002 body:** similar — investigate how the operator should configure artifact traffic routing from main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance; bounded outcomes: (A) gateway/HTTPRoute-level routing with no tracking-server change; (B) tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. Deliverable: routing design decision. Note this is the gate for the conditional branch epic.\n\n**E003 body:** as planned. Note dependency in plain terms: builds on the plugin workspace resolution capability functioning in the artifacts-only context, and on the initialization-coupling investigation findings.\n\n**E004 body:** verify and extend plugin.\n\n**E005 body:** operator topology.\n\n**E006 body:** integration validation.\n\n**BRANCH-B-E006 body:** tracking-server delegation.\n\nSignal files with tables.\n\nNow — one more re-check of \"no cross-references to sibling epics\" in bodies: I must not write \"E001\" etc. I'll refer to \"the initialization-coupling investigation\" / \"the routing-approach investigation\" / \"the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator\" etc. Also must not mention branch/epic IDs in bodies. OK.\n\nAlso HLR references: \"HLR-1\" is a strategy HLR id, not a sibling epic — that's required (HLR Traceability section). Fine.\n\nLet me also double check E003's title/scope doesn't prescribe implementation details beyond strategy (\"decompose, don't design\"). The strategy itself specifies flags, path structure, 403/503 — I mirror those, no invented APIs. Good.\n\nNow, budget: ~$1 used. Each Write + frontmatter set is cheap. Let me write files now.\n\nOrder: summary first (per Step 8a), then epics, then signals, then validate, then set decompose_complete.\n\nActually — one concern: frontmatter.py set on a file without existing frontmatter — need to verify behavior. I'll test with the summary first and read output.\n\nLet me write the summary body now.\n\nAlso the mermaid: keep node labels simple to avoid parse issues — use E001[\"...\"]? Simpler: \n```\ngraph TD\n    E001 --> E004\n    E001 --> E003\n    E004 --> E003\n    E002 --> E005\n    E003 --> E005\n    E003 --> E006\n    E004 --> E006\n```\nWith a legend table below. Clean.\n\nHealth warning wording for E005 size — strategy estimate: \"Operator split-deployment topology ... 2-3 sprints\". \n\nLet me now also prepare E006's scope wording re: routing — \"split-server routing validation is carried by the operator topology and routing epics' acceptance criteria\" — but can't say \"epics\"... I can say \"carried by the operator topology work's acceptance criteria\" in the epic body. In the summary I can reference epic IDs freely (summary is the plan). Only epic BODIES can't reference siblings.\n\nWriting now. I'll do Write calls, then a big bash for frontmatter sets.\n\nFor ai_signals keys, per example: ai_signals.change_specificity=1 etc.\n\nE003 gated_by=E001, gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach=\"...\" — quote the text.\n\nLet me draft all content carefully but compactly. I'll aim for solid, review-ready bodies.\n\nOne more decision — E006 title mentions \"End-to-end\" — fine.\n\nAlso, in E005 scope: include operator validation rejecting configs where artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags (from risk mitigation), single MLflow CR declarative config, conditional HTTPRoute creation via CRD discovery, propagation of workspace flags using existing mechanisms. And artifact traffic routing per the routing-approach investigation outcome (in plain terms: \"the mechanism determined by the routing-approach investigation\").\n\nBRANCH-B-E006 gated_by E002 and in dependencies. Per rule: \"gated_by is always a member of dependencies\". deps=[RHAISTRAT-8009-E002]. ✓ And no main-plan epic lists BRANCH-B-E006 in deps. ✓ (E005 doesn't.)\n\nWrite time.","signature":"9c0eadb710d14453afac9a5822bb9a21"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63710,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94bc8ba55f0f6fae","agent_id":"a9ea81eb8dd2822c4","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"2baeb392-9128-4576-985d-ff0083e9229b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:38:52.882Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
