{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b808caa7-397d-49cd-97ff-51be97f76a01","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac361c0348a37966","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-k_v0du9z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigate workspace-store and auth-plugin initialization in the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution and the `kubernetes://` workspace store can be initialized and exercised in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags this as a genuine unknown (\"needs validation\") in both its assumptions and its dependency table, and its risk register names plugin coupling to full server initialization as a key risk whose answer changes the scope of both the plugin work and the server's initialization sequence for workspace-aware artifact serving. The findings gate the server and plugin implementation work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the plugin's workspace resolution initialization path (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) in the plugin source and the MLflow server source, and identify any dependency on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store can resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping without initialized tracking stores, and what API interactions that resolution requires.\n- Confirm (or refute) that artifact request paths on the artifacts endpoints carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership under the standard S3 artifact store layout (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`).\n- Record a bounded outcome: either workspace resolution already functions in the artifacts-only context (verification only), or it is coupled to full server initialization and requires factoring into an independent initialization path within the plugin (listing the exact coupling points).\n- Deliverable: a findings document with cited source evidence and a verify-or-refactor determination, sufficient to finalize the scope of the plugin extension work and the server's workspace-provider initialization sequence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The findings document states, with file-level source evidence, whether the plugin's workspace resolution initialization depends on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n- The findings document states, with evidence, whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without initialized tracking stores.\n- The findings document records the bounded outcome (works as-is vs coupled-and-needs-refactoring) and, if coupled, lists the specific coupling points that would have to be factored into an independent initialization path.\n- The findings document confirms or refutes that artifact request paths carry experiment/run identifiers sufficient for workspace resolution under the standard S3 artifact store layout, citing the path structure in evidence.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1** (P0, flag composition for workspace-validated artifact serving): this investigation gates the server initialization approach — the answer determines how the server initializes only the workspace provider.\n- **HLR-2** (P0, workspace validation of artifact requests): gates the feasibility of resolving workspace membership per artifact request.\n- **HLR-7** (P1, auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context): this investigation directly determines whether the plugin work is verification-only or requires refactoring.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":84756,"output_tokens":0},"context_management"