rectly when invoked from an artifacts-only server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized.\n- If the initialization-coupling investigation finds that workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so it can be loaded and exercised without tracking stores — while leaving the tracking server's existing path unchanged.\n- Preserve the plugin's existing registration mechanism (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`).\n- Keep the authentication layer unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup work identically for the artifacts-only instance and the main tracking deployment; no changes to authentication.\n- Provide test evidence of workspace resolution succeeding and failing correctly (member vs non-member) from the artifacts-only context.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The plugin resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping from artifact request context in an artifacts-only server with no tracking or model registry stores initialized, demonstrated by passing tests covering member and non-member scenarios.\n- If coupling was found: workspace resolution is factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin, and the tracking server's existing workspace behavior passes the plugin's existing test suite unchanged (no regression).\n- The plugin continues to register and load through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group / `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` mechanism — no new registration mechanism is introduced.\n- No changes are made to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar setup or the `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication configuration.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-7** (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered here.\n- **HLR-2** (P0, enabling): the server's workspace validation of artifact requests delegates to this plugin's resolution; this epic transitively enables the P0 validation requirement and is therefore P0 by priority inheritance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86327,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94bc8ba55f0f6fae","agent_id":"a9ea81eb8dd2822c4","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"65f23a6c-f86c-4a4f-b91d-46e41d32d5ba","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:40:34.838Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
