{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3ceb0793-c46c-456c-9118-74aa3d5479d1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95bbe7cd6bd637ed","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-k_v0du9z/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E006.md","content":"# Tracking-server artifact operation delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n\n## Description\n\nConditional epic (branch B): this work exists only if the routing-approach investigation determines that the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (outcome B), rather than artifact traffic being routed purely at the Gateway API HTTPRoute level (outcome A). In outcome A this epic is removed — the operator topology work handles routing entirely at the gateway. The epic delivers the tracking-server-side configuration capability that lets the main tracking deployment delegate artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add the tracking-server configuration capability (determined by the routing-approach investigation's outcome B design) that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n- Ensure delegated artifact traffic remains subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — the delegation must not introduce a path that serves artifacts without validation (the split-topology misconfiguration risk named in the strategy).\n- Preserve current behavior when the delegation configuration is absent: the tracking server serves/handles artifacts exactly as today.\n- Provide test evidence of delegation functioning and of the no-delegation default behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The tracking server supports the delegation configuration selected by the routing-approach investigation (outcome B), and with it configured, artifact operations initiated through the main tracking deployment are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n- Delegated artifact requests remain subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — no artifact content is served through the delegation path without workspace validation when workspace-aware mode is active.\n- With no delegation configuration set, the tracking server's artifact handling behavior is unchanged from current behavior.\n- Tests cover the delegated and non-delegated configurations, including the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-6** (P1, conditional): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — this epic delivers the server-side half of that routing if (and only if) the routing-approach investigation resolves to outcome B; the operator-side wiring is delivered by the rewritten operator topology routing work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90128,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94bc8ba55f0f6fae","agent_id":"a9ea81eb8dd2822c4","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"0ed1d3b2-c0e3-437e-ae6b-d3425a2427e1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:41:14.799Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
