{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-812dfff65382a660","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate workspace-store and auth-plugin initialization in the artifacts-only\n4\t  server context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigate workspace-store and auth-plugin initialization in the artifacts-only server context\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves whether the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution and the `kubernetes://` workspace store can be initialized and exercised in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags this as a genuine unknown (\"needs validation\") in both its assumptions and its dependency table, and its risk register names plugin coupling to full server initialization as a key risk whose answer changes the scope of both the plugin work and the server's initialization sequence for workspace-aware artifact serving. The findings gate the server and plugin implementation work.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Trace the plugin's workspace resolution initialization path (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) in the plugin source and the MLflow server source, and identify any dependency on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n35\t- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store can resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping without initialized tracking stores, and what API interactions that resolution requires.\n36\t- Confirm (or refute) that artifact request paths on the artifacts endpoints carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership under the standard S3 artifact store layout (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`).\n37\t- Record a bounded outcome: either workspace resolution already functions in the artifacts-only context (verification only), or it is coupled to full server initialization and requires factoring into an independent initialization path within the plugin (listing the exact coupling points).\n38\t- Deliverable: a findings document with cited source evidence and a verify-or-refactor determination, sufficient to finalize the scope of the plugin extension work and the server's workspace-provider initialization sequence.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- The findings document states, with file-level source evidence, whether the plugin's workspace resolution initialization depends on tracking-store or model-registry-store initialization.\n43\t- The findings document states, with evidence, whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without initialized tracking stores.\n44\t- The findings document records the bounded outcome (works as-is vs coupled-and-needs-refactoring) and, if coupled, lists the specific coupling points that would have to be factored into an independent initialization path.\n45\t- The findings document confirms or refutes that artifact request paths carry experiment/run identifiers sufficient for workspace resolution under the standard S3 artifact store layout, citing the path structure in evidence.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- **HLR-1** (P0, flag composition for workspace-validated artifact serving): this investigation gates the server initialization approach — the answer determines how the server initializes only the workspace provider.\n50\t- **HLR-2** (P0, workspace validation of artifact requests): gates the feasibility of resolving workspace membership per artifact request.\n51\t- **HLR-7** (P1, auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context): this investigation directly determines whether the plugin work is verification-only or requires refactoring.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc6d5e2a099eed6","agent_id":"a1d712262287d63fb","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"a02173b6-ce35-4296-a233-8bed8bd88629","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:45.458Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-812dfff65382a660","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
