{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-935c6a8ea520d793","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: End-to-end multi-tenant validation of workspace-aware artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: 1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 5\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# End-to-end multi-tenant validation of workspace-aware artifact serving\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the automated end-to-end validation of workspace-aware artifact serving across the server and auth plugin components, covering the strategy's multi-tenant acceptance scenarios: workspace member access, cross-workspace denial, fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable, backwards compatibility, and single-tenant regression. The strategy's effort estimate budgets 1-2 sprints for integration testing (multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility, single-tenant regression, fail-closed edge cases); this epic is that work stream, producing a reusable scenario suite that runs against a realistic multi-tenant environment with the kubernetes-auth authentication, the `kubernetes://` workspace store, and S3 artifact storage. It owns the strategy's end-to-end acceptance criteria 1-4 (the operator topology's reconciliation criteria are carried by the operator work, and split-server routing validation is carried by the operator topology and routing work).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- An automated multi-tenant scenario suite covering: a workspace member successfully retrieving an artifact from their workspace's experiment (HTTP 200 with correct content); a member of one workspace denied an artifact belonging to another workspace's experiment (HTTP 403 with insufficient-permissions error); the workspace-aware artifacts-only instance denying requests when the workspace store is unreachable (HTTP 503, fail-closed); and artifacts-only serving without workspace flags preserving current behavior (HTTP 200 regardless of workspace membership).\n40\t- Single-tenant regression scenarios: deployments that do not set `--enable-workspaces` retain current artifact-serving behavior.\n41\t- Backwards-compatibility scenarios: omitting either flag (`--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces`, or `--enable-workspaces` without `--artifacts-only`) preserves current behavior.\n42\t- Fail-closed edge cases: transient workspace store unavailability, invalid or missing workspace context in requests (denied, not served).\n43\t- The suite runs the artifacts-only server with the combined flag configuration against the kubernetes-auth plugin, the `kubernetes://` workspace store, and the S3 artifact store (the standard RHOAI configuration), exercising the plugin's workspace resolution end-to-end.\n44\t- Results reported per scenario with pass/fail status, usable as release evidence for the multi-tenant isolation requirement.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- The scenario suite passes end-to-end: a member of workspace A retrieving an artifact of an experiment in workspace A through the workspace-aware artifacts-only instance receives HTTP 200 with the correct artifact content.\n49\t- The scenario suite passes the denial case: a member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting an artifact of an experiment in workspace B receives HTTP 403 with an error indicating insufficient workspace permissions.\n50\t- The scenario suite passes the fail-closed case: with the workspace store (Kubernetes API) unreachable, artifact requests are denied with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable.\n51\t- The scenario suite passes the no-flags case: with `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, any authenticated user's artifact request returns HTTP 200 regardless of workspace membership (current behavior preserved).\n52\t- Single-tenant regression and backwards-compatibility scenarios pass: deployments without workspace flags exhibit current artifact-serving behavior.\n53\t- All scenarios execute against an environment using the kubernetes-auth authentication plugin, the `kubernetes://` workspace store, and the S3 artifact store, and produce a per-scenario pass/fail report.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4** (P0): this epic provides the end-to-end verification of these requirements — the strategy acceptance criteria 1-4 are owned here as measurable scenarios.\n58\t- **HLR-8** (P2): the denial scenarios verify that workspace access denials are recorded in the server logs.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc6d5e2a099eed6","agent_id":"a1d712262287d63fb","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"426df062-eba4-42bd-8d7d-88792a07205a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:49.257Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-935c6a8ea520d793","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
