{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5880f04ef126ba6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Tracking-server artifact operation delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only\n4\t  instance\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If gateway-level HTTPRoute routing suffices (outcome A), no tracking-server\n17\t    delegation change is needed and this epic is removed; routing is handled entirely\n18\t    by the operator topology work.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Tracking-server artifact operation delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional epic (branch B): this work exists only if the routing-approach investigation determines that the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (outcome B), rather than artifact traffic being routed purely at the Gateway API HTTPRoute level (outcome A). In outcome A this epic is removed — the operator topology work handles routing entirely at the gateway. The epic delivers the tracking-server-side configuration capability that lets the main tracking deployment delegate artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Add the tracking-server configuration capability (determined by the routing-approach investigation's outcome B design) that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n44\t- Ensure delegated artifact traffic remains subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — the delegation must not introduce a path that serves artifacts without validation (the split-topology misconfiguration risk named in the strategy).\n45\t- Preserve current behavior when the delegation configuration is absent: the tracking server serves/handles artifacts exactly as today.\n46\t- Provide test evidence of delegation functioning and of the no-delegation default behavior.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The tracking server supports the delegation configuration selected by the routing-approach investigation (outcome B), and with it configured, artifact operations initiated through the main tracking deployment are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n51\t- Delegated artifact requests remain subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — no artifact content is served through the delegation path without workspace validation when workspace-aware mode is active.\n52\t- With no delegation configuration set, the tracking server's artifact handling behavior is unchanged from current behavior.\n53\t- Tests cover the delegated and non-delegated configurations, including the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **HLR-6** (P1, conditional): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — this epic delivers the server-side half of that routing if (and only if) the routing-approach investigation resolves to outcome B; the operator-side wiring is delivered by the rewritten operator topology routing work.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cc6d5e2a099eed6","agent_id":"a1d7122622