{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ee8211e7a053466","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing approach for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing approach for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy poses this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. It has two bounded outcomes, and the answer changes what the operator topology work builds and whether additional server-side work exists.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Determine whether Gateway API HTTPRoute rules can distinguish artifact API traffic from other tracking/registry traffic at the ingress level and route it to the dedicated artifacts-only instance's Service, without any tracking-server change — including how the artifacts endpoints' paths are matched and what happens to non-artifact traffic.\n34\t- Determine whether the tracking server instead requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance (i.e., whether artifact request handling inside the tracking server cannot be bypassed at the gateway level), and what that delegation would look like.\n35\t- Evaluate both options against the security requirement that artifact traffic must not be able to bypass workspace validation (a misrouted path that serves artifacts without validation is the split-topology risk named in the strategy).\n36\t- Assess compatibility with the operator's existing conditional Gateway API integration (runtime CRD discovery).\n37\t- Record the bounded outcome: (A) gateway/HTTPRoute-level routing suffices with no tracking-server change, or (B) the tracking server needs a delegation configuration change. The outcome selects the conditional branch for the routing implementation and is recorded as a routing design decision document.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- The routing design decision document states which bounded outcome holds, with evidence from the operator source, Gateway API routing semantics, and the tracking server's artifact request handling.\n42\t- The document identifies the concrete routing mechanism for the selected outcome (HTTPRoute rule design or tracking-server delegation configuration) and its implications for the split-server topology.\n43\t- The document demonstrates that the selected mechanism cannot route artifact traffic in a way that bypasses workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance, or identifies the guardrails required to prevent it.\n44\t- The document states the compatibility of the selected mechanism with the operator's existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API resources.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- **HLR-6** (P1, main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance): this investigation determines the mechanism and design of that routing, and whether additional server-side delegation work is required.\n49\t- **HLR-5** (P1, dedicated artifacts-only instance with its own Service and HTTPRoute): the routing outcome affects the HTTPRoute design for the split-server topology.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2b7d2cee52897d","agent_id":"aaf7aa26bf677378d","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"84c725fa-a72e-4a0a-90c1-2dc2a6eac02a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:49:03.867Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ee8211e7a053466","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
