{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c009966ec36572","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds workspace resolution is not coupled\n15\t    to tracking-store initialization, this epic collapses to verification with test\n16\t    evidence; if coupled, scope expands to factoring resolution into an independent\n17\t    initialization path within the plugin.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic verifies and extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`; the artifacts-only server needs to call the same workspace resolution logic before proxying artifact requests to the storage backend. Whether the plugin works in this context as-is or requires refactoring is determined by the initialization-coupling investigation; this epic's scope flexes accordingly (verification with evidence, or refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path). The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged — authentication at the ingress level works identically for both the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance. Per the Staff Engineer input, workspace authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure; this epic does not prescribe Kubernetes API mechanics (e.g., no SelfSubjectAccessReview prescription) — the plugin's existing authorization model is reused as-is for artifact request validation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify that the plugin's workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the workspace store) functions correctly when invoked from an artifacts-only server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized.\n44\t- If the initialization-coupling investigation finds that workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so it can be loaded and exercised without tracking stores — while leaving the tracking server's existing path unchanged.\n45\t- Preserve the plugin's existing registration mechanism (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`).\n46\t- Keep the authentication layer unchanged: the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup work identically for the artifacts-only instance and the main tracking deployment; no changes to authentication.\n47\t- Provide test evidence of workspace resolution succeeding and failing correctly (member vs non-member) from the artifacts-only context.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The plugin resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping from artifact request context in an artifacts-only server with no tracking or model registry stores initialized, demonstrated by passing tests covering member and non-member scenarios.\n52\t- If coupling was found: workspace resolution is factored into an independent initialization path within the plugin, and the tracking server's existing workspace behavior passes the plugin's existing test suite unchanged (no regression).\n53\t- The plugin continues to register and load through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group / `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` mechanism — no new registration mechanism is introduced.\n54\t- No changes are made to the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar setup or the `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication configuration.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-7** (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — delivered here.\n59\t- **HLR-2** (P0, enabling): the server's workspace validation of artifact requests delegates to this plugin's resolution; this epic transitively enables the P0 validation requirement and is therefore P0 by priority inheritance.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba2b7d2cee52897d","agent_id":"aaf7aa26bf677378d","session_id":"4ef6c81f-5e30-4fc1-86dc-31c77ed3b7ca","uuid":"d7f459c1-bb4e-40c4-9446-836f960bebc5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:49:06.659Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c009966ec36572","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
