{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be98d215994dd190","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signal Rationale — RHAISTRAT-8009-E001 (Investigation)\n2\t\n3\tInvestigation epics use the 5-signal `investigation_signals` set.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| question_specificity | 1 | Concrete, enumerable questions with definable pass/fail criteria: does the plugin's workspace resolution initialization depend on tracking/model-registry store initialization; can the `kubernetes://` workspace store resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking stores; do artifact request paths carry experiment/run identifiers under the standard S3 layout. Each has a binary answer verifiable from source. |\n8\t| source_accessibility | 1 | The answer is determined by readable artifacts: the mlflow server source, the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins source, and the workspace store implementation — all in team-accessible repositories. The answer exists in the code today; nothing is pending an unmade decision. |\n9\t| local_runnability | 0 | The mlflow server and plugin are pip-installable Python and can run locally, but the `kubernetes://` workspace store resolution genuinely requires a Kubernetes API server to exercise end-to-end, so the full question cannot be answered by local binary/library execution alone (source analysis can answer the coupling question; runtime confirmation needs a cluster). |\n10\t| cluster_hardware_dependence | -1 | The gating question (initialization-path coupling) is answerable from source. Peripheral confirmation — exercising workspace resolution against the `kubernetes://` store in an artifacts-only context — needs a live cluster. No GPU or prod-scale hardware is needed. |\n11\t| human_judgment_required | 0 | No stakeholder, product, or external-party decision is needed; the unknown is a technical fact about the codebase that the investigation resolves directly. |\n