{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e26750773daa68","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signal Rationale — RHAISTRAT-8009-E003 (Implementation)\n2\t\n3\tImplementation epics use the 9-signal `ai_signals` set.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| change_specificity | 1 | The strategy specifies exact flags (`--artifacts-only`, `--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`), the artifact path structure (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), and exact behaviors (HTTP 403 on denial, HTTP 503 fail-closed, fail-to-start without store URI). |\n8\t| pattern_precedent | 1 | The tracking server already implements workspace validation for non-artifact operations behind `--enable-workspaces` and an artifacts-only proxy mode; this change extends both existing paths rather than inventing a new one. |\n9\t| adapter_pattern | 1 | Follows the existing reference implementation: authorization is delegated to the existing auth plugin infrastructure (`--app-name kubernetes-auth`, workspace store), per the strategy and Staff Engineer input. |\n10\t| existing_foundation | 1 | Extends existing flags, existing artifact request handling, and the existing workspace store integration — no greenfield surface. |\n11\t| open_questions | 0 | The one design dependency (workspace provider initialization decoupling) is resolved by the gating investigation before this epic starts, and its outcome selects only among initialization sequences that this epic consumes as input — it does not change the implementation approach. Unlike the plugin and operator epics, where the equivalent gate determines the shape of the work (verification-only vs refactor; routing-mechanism selection), this epic's entire contract is pinned by the strategy before the gate resolves: the exact flags (`--artifacts-only`, `--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`), the artifact path structure, and the observable behaviors (HTTP 403